\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{Begin with a text format and renderer for validated elementary shapes. General molecule import, interactive editing, and external interchange are optional clients after the corresponding presentation and typing checks exist.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{A drawing should round-trip to checked boundary data.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rejected}
  \p{Letting a renderer's limitations determine the mathematical shape category.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Acceptance}
  \p{Round-trip and invalid-boundary examples for each activated format.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{later except the small \ref{ms-foundation} examples.}
}
